      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T18:24:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that the OLT Device Handler\u0027s \u0027send_proxy_message()\u0027 method will first need to check if it is okay to send.  We do this in the Adtran DA by checking.\n  1. Is the PON enabled\n  2. Is the ONU ID valid on the pon.\n\nFor #2, when I activate an ONU, I basically have an ONU object that is saved in a PON dictionary.  For the OpenOLT, this looks like it is also done in the openolt_data_model code.\n\nFor other non-OpenOLT derived OLTs (microsemi, CIG, Tibit) we may need to coordinate the change.\n\nI am fairly sure that the Tibit will be able to support this method in the near future (sometime after lockdown).",
